title: An Infantile Disorder
subtitle: Lenin writes about the German left.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1920 and month = 6 and crisis = 0 and e20_election_done = 1 and ending_id = 0
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.e20_lead_ul = (Q.leading_faction == 'ultraleft') ? 1 : 0;
!}

= An Infantile Disorder

A pamphlet arrives from Moscow: *"Left-Wing" Communism: An Infantile Disorder*, by Lenin. It is aimed at the communists of every country who refuse to work in the unions and the parliaments, and above all at the Germans. To stay out of the reactionary unions, Lenin writes, is to leave the backward masses under the influence of the reactionary leaders.

[? if wg_stance = 1 : In an appendix he turns to our March statement on a loyal opposition to a workers' government, and calls it correct in its basic premise. ?][? if wg_stance != 1 : In an appendix he says that a communist party should have offered a loyal opposition to a workers' government in March. ?] [? if e20_lead_ul = 1 : Every page reads like an indictment of our own Zentrale. ?][? if kapd_exists = 1 : The KAPD's leaders call it a betrayal. ?]

- @print: Print it in a hundred thousand copies.
- @unions: Send the whole party back into the unions.
- @wrong: Reply that Lenin is wrong about Germany.

@print
subtitle: Lenin is on our side of the argument, and he says so in print.
on-arrival: {!
Q.ultraleft_satisfaction -= 6;
if (Q.kapd_exists) { Q.kapd_members -= 3; RG.district('berlin', {members: 0.05}); }
RG.ecci('lenin', 6);
!}

The pamphlet sells at every party meeting. [? if kapd_exists = 1 : In Berlin a few hundred KAPD members read it and come back to us. ?]

@unions
subtitle: [? if lock_union_work = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] A communist fraction in every union branch.
choose-if: lock_union_work < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids work inside the reformist unions.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_union_work == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.worker_support += 3;
Q.ultraleft_satisfaction -= 10;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

Every member who left a union is told to rejoin it. In Chemnitz, Brandler has been doing this for a year.

@wrong
subtitle: Moscow will not forget it.
view-if: ultraleft_gone = 0 or e20_lead_ul = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.independence += 8;
Q.lean_ultraleft += 2;
RG.ecci('lenin', -10);
!}

Our reply says Germany has a proletariat of millions and does not need Moscow to explain the unions to it. Zinoviev answers in *Pravda*.
